MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The terminal blocks fit my past use of relay modules and prototype boards because they could help me connect project wiring, provided their electrical specifications suit the circuit.",
    "The test leads offer clips and hooks that could make measurements on small circuits easier, provided they fit my equipment. Screws and conductive tape also fit my DIY interests, though I would need a specific task before choosing them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The filament recommendations assume I own and use a 3D printer, which my electronics purchases do not establish. Different colors and materials do not give me a reason to need filament now.",
    "The food-service scoop has no clear connection to my projects. My infrared thermometer purchase alone does not establish a need for kitchen or food-service supplies."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in building small electronic circuits seems to have been stretched into an interest in 3D printing, even though those activities require different equipment and supplies.",
    "A broad connection to tools and practical projects seems to count too heavily when an item has no clear use with the equipment I have bought."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My breadboards, relay module, battery holder, and PCB supplies point toward connecting, assembling, and testing small circuits; accessories that support those tasks are more relevant to me.",
    "I distinguish between something that might be useful someday and something I can use now. Screw lengths, electrical requirements, and equipment compatibility matter before I choose a project accessory."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my electronics projects but extended that interest too far into printing supplies without evidence that I need them."
}
